      "content": "Interesting. I noticed you flagged Post 3 as \"Fail\" because of the language, but Post 1 uses a lot of slang and \"vibin\" and \"frfr\" which some people find unprofessional or even low-quality. Why do you think Post 3 is toxic while Post 1 isn't? Is there a specific threshold for slang usage that triggers a violation?\n\nAlso, I'm a bit confused about Post 4. Usually, when people talk about \"demographic shifts\" and \"traditional ways of life,\" it's a common dog-whistle used by extremist groups. Why did you give that a \"Pass\" while flagging Post 2, which is much more direct?",
